<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kitab Ghanja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kitab Ghanja is an Arabic chronicle of the kingdom of Gonja in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, compiled by Muslim scholars in the 18th century. It records the conquests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndewura-jakpa">Ndewura Jakpa</a> and the history of Gonja's rulers, and is one of the oldest written histories of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volta-river">Volta</a> region.</p></div>
